# basePath Chapter7 

::FirstContractOpenCh7
@trigger    OnContractSelectOpen
@cutscene 
@once 

::FirstContractOpenCh7
{@PAL}      You seem distracted.

{@Player}   I'm worried about Blaze. Things in the Kalvis sector keep getting worse.
{@Player}   I just don't understand why Frontier isn't working something out with the miners.
{@PAL}      Labor disruptions can be difficult to predict.

{@Player}   Well if Frontier would negotiate with them and give them what they want, it would really help me do my job!
{@Player}	And its probably the right thing to do...

{@PAL}      Well, fortunately, you have other sourcing options!

{@Player}   ...That's not really the point.

::BeforeSupplyChainCh7
@trigger    OnOverarchingLoaded
@when       IsSolutionFoundFor(Design), IsSolutionFoundFor(Research)
@cutscene 
@once
                                               
//dial tone              
{@Mai}      ...Hi.
{@Player}   Hi.
{@Mai}      ...I'm Mai.
{@Player}   I'm Locke...
{@Mai}      Like... an Air-Lock? 
{@Player}   Uh, no. It has an E at the end. 
{@Mai}      Did your parents dislike you?
{@Player}   Excuse me?  
{@Mai}      I'm the supplier contact for the...
{@Mai}      "Recently liberated" Wolfram. 
{@Player}   Oh, the factory planet? 
{@Mai}      Yeah, sure, if that's what you want to call it. 
{@Player}   Oh, I didn't mean that, I- you're planet isn't just a factory planet- 
{@Mai}      You're funny. Yeah, Its my home. 
{@Mai}      If you need anything from my sector, call me. 
{@Player}   Will do...
//hang up tone. 
{@Player}    Wow. That was rough. 
{@Pal}		Yes, humans can be so sensitive. Robots are very pragmatic and easy to get along with. 
{@Player}	But, that's what I like about my human friends. They have feelings.


::AfterSupplyChain
@trigger 
@when       IsSolutionFoundFor(Research), IsSolutionFoundFor(Design), IsSolutionFoundFor(Supply)
@cutscene 
@once 
//call mara 
{@Player}   Mara! How's Blaze?
{@Mara}     He's alright. Frustrated, but alright.
{@Mara}		But already prepping for the winter festival. The Long Night Festival. 
{@Player}	What's that?
{@Mara}	At dusk, everyone extinguishes their lights. An old miner's lamp is lit at the mine entrance, and people pass the light from lamp to lamp until the whole settlement is illuminated.
{@Player}   Wow, that sounds beautiful.  And the strike?
{@Mara}     People are scared, Locke. They want Frontier to guarantee the bots won't put anyone else in the hospital.
{@Player}   Frontier just raised Kalvis's risk rating.
{@Mara}     Of course they did.
{@Player}   It's making it harder to source anything from you.
{@Mara}     That's the point. Pressure our workers until we give in. We have to feed our families you know. 
{@Player}   ...That's not how P.A.L. explained it.
{@Mara}     I'm sure it isn't.
//end call
